  "courseBefore": "Learn data engineering from the ground up using simple explanations, runnable examples, practical labs and a complete capstone. The course starts with pipelines, storage, SQL, Python and dimensional modelling, then moves into Azure foundations, Apache Spark, Microsoft Fabric, OneLake, Lakehouse, Data Factory, Real-Time Intelligence with KQL, security, lifecycle management, monitoring and optimization. Version 1.1 aligns the curriculum to Microsoft's DP-700 skills measured as of October 19, 2026 and requires learners to build, troubleshoot and optimize rather than only memorize concepts.",
  "courseAfter": "Learn data engineering from the ground up using simple explanations, runnable examples, practical labs and a complete capstone. The course starts with pipelines, storage, SQL, Python and dimensional modelling, then moves into Azure foundations, Apache Spark, Microsoft Fabric, OneLake, Lakehouse, Data Factory, Real-Time Intelligence with KQL, security, lifecycle management, monitoring and optimization. Version 1.1.1 corrects selected examples and links to the current official DP-700 study guide and requires learners to build, troubleshoot and optimize rather than only memorize concepts.",
